<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <title>grid selector</title>
  <meta charset="utf-8"/>
</head>
<body>
<ol>
  <li id="2" class="h1" au="2">
   intro
    <ol>
      <li id="16">gridSelector contraption</li>
      <li id="17">we will show how it works</li>
      <li id="18">see how incredibly easy it is to make a paint program</li>
      <li id="19">hardly any code at all</li>
      <li id="48" class="h2">
       the paint program
        <ol>
          <li id="49">canvas already does it</li>
          <li id="50">just set the pen and brush</li>
        </ol>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li id="12" class="h1">
   challenge: draw a grid
    <ol>
      <li id="51" class="h2">
       challenge: how would you do it?
        <ol>
          <li id="20">we need to know how many lines to make, and how far apart to make them</li>
          <li id="24">i tend to call this gwh for grid width and height</li>
          <li id="22">then we can divide the canvas size by the cell size to get the number of cells in each dimension</li>
        </ol>
      </li>
      <li id="67" class="h2">
       parameters
        <ol>
          <li id="68">gwh</li>
          <li id="69">cwh</li>
          <li id="70">you can divide the canvas size by one of these to get the other</li>
        </ol>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li id="29" class="h1">
   drawing with lines
    <ol>
      <li id="34">how would you do it by hand?</li>
      <li id="32">first draw vertical lines</li>
      <li id="33">then draw horizontal</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li id="30" class="h1">
   drawing with rectangles
    <ol>
      <li id="31">instead of this we use cross</li>
      <li id="25">now we can loop through the cells and draw a box for each one</li>
      <li id="26">use sleep[5] to illustrate</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li id="35" class="h1">
   why use cross?
    <ol>
      <li id="27">each box maps to an index</li>
      <li id="40">can use the index to easily choose what to draw</li>
      <li id="57">draw numbers</li>
      <li id="36">draw colors</li>
      <li id="37">draw brushes</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li id="64" class="h1">the scaled canvas trick</li>
  <li id="60" class="h1">
   pointer coordinates
    <ol>
      <li id="59">okay so we can draw a grid, and now we want to make it interactive</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li id="61" class="h1">
   pointer to grid coordinates
    <ol>
      <li id="58">the math isn&apos;t that hard</li>
      <li id="66">just divide by gwh</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li id="43" class="h1">grid coords to index</li>
  <li id="44" class="h1">drawing the cursor</li>
  <li id="47" class="h1">
   bundling the contraption
    <ol>
      <li id="46" class="h2">hidden fields</li>
      <li id="75" class="h2">the draw script</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li id="79" class="h1">
   call to action
    <ol>
      <li id="80">before we cover the paint program</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li id="76" class="h1">
   paint program
    <ol>
      <li id="78">bye!</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
</ol>
</body>
</html>
